> Does anyone have any experience with using DEC as a support provider with
> non-DEC equipment?  We're looking into them as a support provider of
> high-end PC-servers (e.g. Oracle application servers).  Specifically,
> looking at how they provide on-site support, timely resolution of broken
> components, 24-hour support (HW & SW).  If any experience, please email or
> respond here.  Thanks.

We use Digital to support our CMD equipment - both BI-SCSI adapters as well as
the CMD CI-SCSI adapter - plus our SI disk drives.  No problems so far.  Once
Digital agrees to support the product (usually subject to local office
approval), you'll get almost the same support level as you get with
Digital-manufactured equipment.  Digital usually has agreements with the
manufacturers for support if they can't get the failure resolved, but we've
never seen this in action.  For every product that Digital supports, there is a
*documented* support plan.  If you're uneasy with Digital's ability to support
the product, contact your local Field Service Manager and ask to see the plan.

