NNTP-Posting-Host: denali.ccs.neu.edu
X-Newsreader: TIN [version 1.2 PL2]

There are two instructions in the Alpha architecture for doing 64x64=128-bit
multiplication:

MULQ Ra,Rb,Rc  puts the lsb 64 bits of Ra*Rb into Rc
UMULH Ra,Rb,Rc puts the msb 64 bits of Ra*Rb into Rc, with the multiplication
               unsigned; two subtractions are needed to get the signed result

This says nothing about whether a particular compiler or OS uses these
instructions.

