In article <goluboff.788736586@rmchep.Colorado.EDU>, goluboff@rmchep.Colorado.EDU (Mariano Goluboff) writes:
|>Hello, 
|>	I have been having some problems with this machine that I just
|>upgraded from Ultrix 4.2a to 4.4. Specifically, when I type pwd as
|>unpriviledged user, I get:
|>pwd: getwd: No such file or directory
|>	If I do it as super-user, I get /, when it should be /home, or
|>whatever the directory is. It happens sometimes in one filesystem,
|>sometimes in another, just at random.
|>
|>Any ideas, ways to fix it?

Known bug.  There is a patch available for it from your local CSC.

Patch id:       ULTV44-020-3

Under ULTRIX V4.4, several commands and utilities will fail with:

getwd: No such file or directory

The problem has been isolated to the getwd() system call detecting an
unresolved link when traversing back up the tree.  The unresolved links are
normal and can be created by automount, leftover from a removed mountpoint
or by a customer's application.

This problem could also be experienced if the getcwd() library call is
used.

