In article <1994Dec28.120617.104@thehulk>, munroe@dmc.com writes:
=OpenVMS/AXP 1.5 ignores the UAF setting for PRCLM in favor of the sysgen
=parameter PQL_MPRCLM.

ANY version of VMS should do that.  That SYSGEN parameter specifies the minimum 
value for PRCLM for any process created.

=If I reduce the sysgen parameter to 0, I get the right
=effect wrt to authorize, but Motif won't start.  In other words, if
=PQL_MPRCLM=10 and authorize for a user FOO has prclm set to 0, when user FOO
=logs in, the prclm is 10, NOT 0.

=How do I turn off the capability for a user to use the SPAWN DCL command and
=LIB$SPAWN RTL routine on a case by case basis and lets me start motif?

Don't give the users in question TMPMBX priv.  This will prevent them from
spawning subprocesses.  It will, unfortunately, also prevent them from creating
temporary mailboxes for other purposes.

PQL_MPRCLM is a dynamic SYSGEN parameter.  Hence, you could have it set to 10
in your CURRENT parameter database, and have your startup procedure set it to 0
in the ACTIVE parameter database after MOTIF is started.

I don't know whether the latter would fix your problem; that would depend on
whether when someone logs in using MOTIF, their job spawns subprocesses.
