 00000: ffd8 ffe0 0010 4a46 4946 0001 0100 0001  ......JFIF......
 00010: 0001 0000 ffdb 0043 0003 0202 0302 0203  .......C........

I don't know if this corresponds to a special character sequence in
some NFS protocol, but if the DECstation is serving the file, I get
time-out errors on SGI clients when I try to load it.  You might be
asking if this is really what's happening, and whether the problem
