>In article <1994Dec16.174151.1020@acavax.lynchburg.edu>,
teague@acavax.lynchburg.edu (Kipp) writes:
>|>
>|>I am attempting to connect a modem with a standard RS232 connector (25 pin)
>|>to an Ethernet Communications Server which uses Digital's 8-pin connector
>|>and I am unable to determine the pin out configuration used by the server
>|>for the 8-pin connector.  Can anyone assist?


Pinout for DECserver 700-16 is as follows

Pin                Function           Default

1                  RXD GND
2                  RXD
3                  TXD GND
4                  CTS                  CTS
                   RI
5                  RTS                  RTS
                   DSRS
6                  TXD
7                  DTR
8                  DSR                  DSR
                   DCD

Pins 4,5 and 8 are software configurable between CTS/RTS/DSR and RI/DSRS/DCD.
For RS-232, pins 1 and 3 should be connected to each other.


