[ Sorry for any duplicate posts on this. My news server hicked up 
during an earlier attempt. (Already provided answer my mail) ]

This is a relativly widly known VMS system management gotcha.
It has been discussed a few times in the comp.os.vms newsgroup.
I would suggest to check out the entries there and if continue
the discussion there if needed.


	
Additional information:
	- for an explanation, $help/message headerful
	- for temporary relief, $purge as many files as possible.
	- to prevent the problem, $init disks with adequate /header value.
	- to anticipate the problem, verify 'map area in use' from:
		$dump/header/block=count=0 disk:[000000]indexf.sys

 HEADERFULL,  file header is full

  Facility:     SYSTEM, System Services

  Explanation:  The file header map area on the volume is full and cannot
                be extended. This error occurs only when the file header
                extension is inhibited, for example, when the index file is
                being extended.

  User Action:  Compress the volume by copying it with BACKUP.

Hope this helps,		+--------------------------------------+
