>Quite right.  In the interest of brevity, my previous post didn't list *all*
>the stupid marketing decisions that DEC made with its PCs.  But many people
>at the time did note the irony:  Digital, whose PDP-11 had been such a great
>success partly because of its open architecture (you could by Unibus goodies
>and Qbus goodies from a whole bunch of third-party vendors) gave us PCs with
