And suffer they did!  Things just went downhill from the PC days.  
Remember the MicroVAX II?  DEC's original game plan was to license the 
CPU to OEMs, and the company in fact had deals lined up with several 
licensees.  About a month before the product launch, DEC in its infinite 
wisdom decided to scuttle the deals and adopt a xenophobic stance.  Which 
they maintained through subsequent gaffes like MSCP disks, the evil VAXBI 
bus and similar antedeluvian throwbacks which are best forgotten.

I've always liked DEC products, but until quite recently, the firm's 
marketeers have displayed a unique ability to shoot themselves in both 
feet with one bullet.  It will be interesting to see how the Multia issue 
plays out.  With apologies to the Firesign Theatre, the current Multia 
stance looks like an open-and-shut case of "Forward Into The Past"!


