The MMJ pinout on the DECserver family of products ended with the
DECserver 300 which has not shipped for several years.  Starting with
the DECserver 700-16 we went to the RJ-45 (also known as MJ8) connector
so that more signaling could be added and to make the system more
compatible with the Open DECconnect wiring system.  This connector can
now be found on the DECservers 700-16, 90TL, 90M, and the 900TM.  It is
also used as a console port on many of the DEChub 900 products.  Pinout
for the DECserver 700-16 and 900TM is:

1  RXD GND
2  RXD
3  TXD GND
4  CTS OR RI (software selectable, CTS is default)
5  RTS or DSRS (software selectable, RTS is default)
6  TXD
7  DTR
8  DSR or DCD (software selectable, DSR is default)

Pins 4 and 5 are not used on the DECservers 90TL and 90M.  Interface is RS-423.

Loren Albright


