           Port       port    port  Button   thin-wire Ethernet

The basic VS2000 has a moni (black/white) frame buffer on the system board. If
pin 9 is connected to pin 8 on the DB-9 (printer port) connector that will make
it (the DB-9) the console port.  Use a null-modem cable to a VT-terminal to get
at the system. Use 8bit no parity I think the default baud rate is 9600 bps. If
nothing is done to the printer port then the system will require, at a minimum,
the monitor cable with a keyboard plugged in.  The console output will go to
the graphics monitor so it would be good to have one of those too. The reset
button will halt the system. If you have the expansion box on the bottom then
the ports there are for tape and disk.  The only disk that will work is an RD54
(159MB formatted) which is the same as a Maxtor 2190 I think.  Use "test 70" at
the console prompt (>>>) to format a disk.


