To:	UofT users of DEC software

  Digital Equipment Corporation (DEC) recently announced changes to their
Campuswide Software License Grant (CSLG) program. If you use DEC software
now or are considering using DEC software in the future, please read the
following information about the CSLG program.

  The original CSLG program was negotiated between Digital and the
University of Toronto in 1990. Since then UofT users of DEC systems have
been able to run many DEC software products at no cost.

  The new plan will take effect on May 1, 1995. Compared to the existing
plan the most significant change will be the introduction of a annual fee.
The cost will depend on the number of systems participating in the program
(not the number of products). It is expected to be well under $1000 per
system, much less than the cost of corresponding conventional licenses.

  The CSLG program provides annual software licenses and annual rights to
new versions for all layered products included in the CSLG Product List.
Because the CSLG program includes rights to new versions, SNS service is no
longer required; this may save money for some participants. The Product
List includes a very large number of software products which run on the
following DEC platforms:

	OpenVMS VAX		OpenVMS AXP
	DEC OSF/1		DEC OSF/1 AXP
	Ultrix/VAX		Ultrix/RISC
	Windows NT

Note that each system must already be licensed to run the base operating
system. Each Product Authorization Key (PAK) will be distributed through
the University's software licensing office. The use of PAKs is DEC's
mechanism for preventing the use of unlicensed software.

  The transition from the present CLSG plan to the new one will take place
over the next few months, as follows:

(1) In the next few weeks University of Toronto Planning and Education
    (UTPE) will be distributing interim PAKs to existing CSLG participants.
    These PAKs will allow all presently licensed software to run through
    the term of the present agreement. The interim PAKs will expire on May
    15, 1995.

(2) In January UTIRC and UTPE will circulate additional information about
    the new CSLG program, organize an open meeting to discuss the issue,
    and identify those who wish to participate in the program.

  In the meantime we will be pleased to answer any questions you may have
about this issue.

