In article <3ctjgl$c0g@jadzia.CSOS.ORST.EDU>, thorpej@basalt.CS.ORST.EDU (Jason R. Thorpe) writes:
>I've acquired several VAXstation 3100s.  I happen to have an Ultrix/VAX
>cd and a DEC cdrom drive.  What I need to know is how do I boot off the cd
>to install the OS?
>

Start by, at the console prompt, type:

	>>> SHOW DEVICE

and see what devices you have.  The CDROM drive will be DKAnnn or DKBnnn
(depending on which SCSI bus into which it's plugged).  Insert the CD into the
drive, and type:

	>>> BOOT DKlnnn

and go from there.

The next question you'll probably be asking is "do I have licenses to run
Ultrix on all these VAXstations?" 

