In article <3c2rfu$bcu@news.duke.edu> Andrew Gallatin,
gallatin@isds.duke.edu writes:
>Alternatively, they could convert their data files using dd & the
>conv=swab option:
>%dd if=file.hp of=file.dec conv=swab
>
I really don't think swab will work for float or 4 byte integers. This
swaps every other pair of bytes, which is o.k. for 2 byte integers. For 4
byte data elements such (integer and float) you need to swap things as
follows:
1,2,3,4->4,3,2,1
This is the way we've been doing swaps between various little endian
(mips, alpha) and
big endian (hp, sun, stardent) platforms for a long time.

