It is, but you have to look in the right man page.  For obvious reasons,
you can't set or delete your environment variables with Unix commands,
you have to do this with shell builtin commands.  So, type

man your_shell

to get the answer.  For (t)csh it's "unsetenv DISPLAY".

Dan 
