> Q:  Does anyone know if DEC has access (ie can use) Silicon Graphics
>     3D software, or, better still, their 3D hardware.
>     While I am at it, what other companies have licences to sell SGI's
>     3D software.

Hi, yes the Alpha should be able to run SGI's 3D software, with some caveats.
Firstly you will need to convert from GL to OpenGl. Then on the Alpha you will
not to have both an Open3D licence AND a graphics accelerator board. The 
default board to come with the Alpha's is HX but that won't work. Another
complication is that I think the ZLZX accelerator boards only run if you
are using unix (OSF) whereas some of the other accelerator boards run on both
OpenVMS and OSF.

ALl of the above is hypothetical. I recently received an Alpha but it has the
default graphics board and I have to wait until 1995 before I can upgrade to
a higher board.

Also, while Open3D works on the Alpha, to run OpenInventor I think you have to
be running OSF.

Hope this is of some help,

Regards,

John






