The Remote Services Console is something you attach to the console port of your
VAX system, and to a free port on the system.  You also attach a console
terminal and a dialup modem to it.

There are various modes.  In one mode, the console terminal is connected to the 
console port, and the modem is connected to the free port on the system.  In
another mode, the modem is connected to the console port.  The idea is to allow
the DDC (Digital Diagnostic Center) (what it was called when the box was built)
to become the console of your system for servicing the system.

Technically speaking, the box does belong to Digital, so you might want to
contact your local Customer Services office and see about returning it.

