My goodness, have you ever actually had to administer an RS/6000 AIX system
for any length of time?  I have never, in fifteen years of administering
Unix systems, seen such a mess as AIX is in right now.  IBM is issuing new
patches at a phenominal rate, virtually every new patch they issue breaks
some other part of the operating system, and they gave up on numbering the
operating system releases over a year ago.  I haven't been thrilled with
the jerking-around that DEC has given their customers over OSF/1, MIPS
system support, and plenty of other things.  But my company is a VAR for
both DEC and IBM, and I am currently responsible for administration and
maintenance on a number of DEC systems (VAX, MIPS and Alpha, Ultrix and
OSF/1) and IBM systems (RS/6000 and RT/PC, AIX 2.2, 3.1 and 3.2), and I
can tell you that there is no comparison between DEC and IBM right now.
