In article <3cj175$epi@styx.uwa.edu.au>, brooker@uniwa.uwa.edu.au (Andrew Brooker) writes:
|>Using version 3.4 of the DEC Fortran on OSF/1 AXP compiler
|>system I get erroneous answers when I try to take non-integer
|>powers of double complex numbers. Does anyone know anything 
|>about this problem?

This was a bug in the math library on OSF/1 V2.0 which is fixed in V3.0,
the current version.  Unfortunately, the math routine was linked into the
compiler for use in compile-time arithmetic, so even if you update just
OSF/1, you may still see the bug.

If you get OSF/1 V3.0 and DEC Fortran V3.5, the bug will go away.
