Has anyone seen or heard of problems like this with an Alphatronix HSC
connected jukebox? If so, is there any resolution? Does anyone have any
ideas on what, if anything, might be wrong with our configuration that is
causing the HSC crashes. I'd appreciate an Email message from any site out
there that is using this subsystem, working or not, so that I can validate
or invalidate Alphatronix's statement that we are the only site with this
problem. 

Here is our configuration and problem history:

The cluster is CI based, and consists of 3 VAX 76XX class systems, an AXP
7610, and 2 4000/VLC workstations, with DSSI, HSJ and Stingray disk drives.
We are running VMS V5.5-2 and AXP V1.5 on the cluster, and Cronic V8.1 on
the HSC. Nothing is connected to the HSC70 except the Emulex requestor card
and Alphatronix Jukebox. We chose the Alphatronix system over others because
it didn't require a custom device driver, and it was CI based instead of
SCSI. We are still looking for a working solution that fits these
parameters.

The primary problem we are having is that the HSC will crash when the robot
changes platters. Among the errors we see from the HSC crashes as reported
by VAXsim are:

			VENUS Bus HSC000 (HSC) Hard
	Count : Explanation
	   24 : 001244 Aborting err rcvry due to excessive timeouts on disk
	   19 : 001444 Unit declared inop-no progress made on CmdRef
	    3 : 000042 Requestor 2 fail INIT DIT
	    2 : 000342 NXM (Trap thru 4)
	   11 : 000402 Reserved Instruction (Trap thru 10)
	   57 : 000602-002005 SW Incon-Periodic K test fail
	   41 : 000602-004073 SW Incon-K not responding Requestor
	    2 : 000602-004076 SW Incon-Port not in DCB err state on DCB err
	   25 : 000602-SW Incon-Unsupported
	   31 : 000204 Unrecvrbl err on disk. Inop. Intervention rqd
	   17 : 000344 Ill bit change in disk sts; EL bit on; so sts logged

Once the HSC crashes, the subsystem will usually not recover itself. Drives
go into Mount Verify, Mount Verify Timeout, etc. and manual corrective
action is required. Sometimes we get drives in these states even without an
HSC crash. Recovery can vary from nothing more than waiting if we are very
lucky (rare), dismounting and remounting drives, to completely stopping all
the Alphatronix software, powering off the HSC and the jukebox, waiting,
powering things back on, running hardware tests on the jukebox, and then
restarting all the software and remounting all the platters. Even this does
not always succeed.

