In article <3bgrvo$k1t@sunb.ocs.mq.edu.au>, vsaparam@laurel.ocs.mq.edu.au (Vasantha Saparamadu) writes:
|>We are looking at upgrading our DEC 5000/240s to Alphas. We want to initially
|>use the existing TX/PIP video card with it rather than buying a J300. We have
|>been told that the PIP is supported for the Alphas. Is there anyone who is
|>actually using this card on the Alphas? Has anyone ported applications such
|>as nv to it?

I scrounged up a TX/PIP to put in one of our DEC 3000 Model 500s here and
it worked fine with the latest version of nv (3.3beta).  Unfortunately,
something in the Sound & Motion J300 support seems to have broken between
3.3alpha and 3.3beta because all the J300 images have a green cast, so
you'll need to stay with 3.3alpha if you are using J300 until someone
can figure out what's broken.

I'm not sure what the 'official' support status of the TX/PIP on the 
DEC 3000s is, because I don't think it was ever formally tested, but it 
does seem to work.

One thing to be careful of when ordering a new DEC 3000 system to use
with your existing TX/PIPs is to make sure that you'll have enough room
in the enclosure for them.  Since they are triple high boards, things
might be a little snug in the desktop enclosures.  You should have plenty
of room in the deskside enclosures.

The TX will probably be a little faster when used with an Alpha system,
but it's still going to be painfully slow if you compare it to something
like the ZLX-E* devices.  If you have another graphics board for
your main screen, you should try to organize things so that you use it
for everything except video capture.

