>-"nroff -man /usr/local/man/man1/mf.1 | less" works without any problems
>or warnings, but is tedious... As far as I can understand "man man" this is
>what man does anyway.

What "man" does is to call:

	tbl man1/mf.1 | nroff -man

and that indeed is bad because that man page already went through tbl
as far as I can tell. Delete the .TS , .TE pair that is wrapped around
that region (starting around 132, ending roughly 100 lines lower down)
and tbl will be happy.

