Most any "well-behaved" SCSI drive will work on our systems, as long as
it's installed correctly (e.g. termination, bus length within spec.
etc.)

OSF will tell you that it sees an RZxx drive out there.  If the drive has
any special features that you want to use (like tagged queueing) then you
will want to go modify the file /sys/data/cam_data.c to add an entry for
the Quantum.  There's a writeup in that file on how to create entries for
new disks.

