Dr. Chris Davis (chris@glueball.physics.louisville.edu) wrote:


: I have a VAX 4000/90 running VMS 5.5.  Currently it has 5.5 GB of disk
: (1 X 3, 2 x 1 plus 400 MB internal system disk).  I would like to add at
: least another 4 GB, maybe 2 x 4GB.  Is there a limit to the amount of disk
: such a machine can handle, either globally or per drive (ie per SCSI slot)?
: If so is the limit defined by VMS or imposed by the architecture of the
: machine (word size etc) ?

No, there is no limit to the number of drives, other than that each SCSI
bus may have only 7 target devices (drives).  I have heard rumors that
a 9 Gb drive doesn't work on some operating system, but the message was
not very specific.  There are also devices that can split one SCSI address,
that's why you have DKA300: drive names.


