Alan Frisbie (frisbie@flying-disk.com) wrote:

: I would like to operate a VAXstation in another room from the
: CPU.   The total distance is about 30 to 40 feet.   Has anyone
: actually done this?   Successfully?

: 1) What did you use for cable?   I have considered buying two
:    25' cables (BC18Z-25), cutting one end off each one and 
:    splicing them together, but consider this a kludge.   Of 
:    course, if the cables were cheap enough, I could overlook 
:    this.   :-)

Yes, we did this.  For the video, we used RG-59 cable, with a male
BNC on one end and a Female BNC on the other, as an extension cord
for the video.  We ran three RG-59 cables tie-wrapped together.
For the mouse, we just cut the mouse cable in the middle and spliced
a suitable cable into it.  For the keyboard, we used thin modular
connectors (like telephone handset connectors) and modular phone cable.
The only problem we ran into is that some systems (notably Vaxstation 3100's)
don't like extensions of more than about 25 feet on the keyboard.  They
get garbling.  If you have this problem, either use a better cable or
make it shorter.

: 2) Is there a "Skunk Box" (BA213) style cabinet kit for the
:    VCB02 (GPX) video board?   (This was originally a VAX 3300
:    which is being modified into a VAXstation 3300.)

Yes, definitely - for the VAXStation 3500 and 3600.  I don't have the
part nomber, however.  Just ask a broker for a cabinet kit for a 3500 or
3600 - you'll get the right part.

: 3) Is there a version of the cable with the 90 degree connector
:    for use in a BA213 style cabinet?

Must be - same comments as above.


