In article <3c2har$q6n@jac.zko.dec.com>,
Steve Lionel <lionel@quark.enet.dec.com> wrote:
>If the application is in Fortran, they can use the CONVERT='BIG_ENDIAN'
>option in the OPEN statement which will cause DEC Fortran to automatically
>do the byte-swap on input or output.  Otherwise it should be a straightforward
>task to write a program to process the file and do the byte swap as
>necessary.

Alternatively, they could convert their data files using dd & the
conv=swab option:
%dd if=file.hp of=file.dec conv=swab

This is admittedly less transparent, but we used this when moving some
researchers from sparcs to Alphas.

BTW- this is assuming OSF/1.

Drew


