john kraft (jkraft@tribble.fhcrc.org) wrote:
: for the following:  MicroVAX II, VAXstation II, and VAXstation 2000, 
: i'm looking for some information.
: what are their VUPS? 
: what kind of hard drives will they take?
: what kind of memory do they take, and in what configurations?
Memory for VS-2000 is little "daughter-cards" that plug on to the system 
board.  DEC, Camintonn and others make them.
MicroVAX II and VAXStation II use the same processor, KA630-AA, and memory
MS630-AA (1 MB), MS630-BA (2 MB), MS630-BB (4 MB), and MS630-CA (8 MB).
The CPU comes with 1 MB on it.  VAXstation II's have either VCB-01 (1024 
x 864 screen, monochrome), or VCB-02 (1024 x 864, 16 or 256 colors).
DEC disk drives are the RD5x series, various makers ST-506 MFM disk drives.
Third party disk controllers support ESDI and SCSI disks.


