The "Gold key" is PF1 on the VT100 keypad.  You shouldn't lash out at DEC
for the fact that most terminal emulators that claim VT100 compatibility
don't have any way to emulate such an essential key.  Many emulators will
allow you to use "F1" as a substitute, but not all do.

I'd like to heap great praise on the maintainers of MS-DOS Kermit and
the author of "GOLD", which together can map the Numlock key on a
PC-clone keyboard (where God intended the Gold key to be) into the
Gold key.  Only a very few commercial terminal emulators come anywhere
close to MS-DOS Kermit in terms of usability, reliability, and
all-around excellence - and MS-DOS Kermit doesn't cost anything! 

