    I'd avoid implementing anything "real" in Macro Assembler (or as it's
    implemented on OpenVMS Alpha, the Macro Compiler) in favor of using
    a language such as C.  When faced with porting Macro code, I would
    consider translating it into C -- a direct port from the assember to
    the compiler is likely quicker (assuming user mode code), but the C
    translation/port is a better long-term solution.


