  Not to comment on the other parts of the message (which I hope will
  find it's way to the appropriate people to read)...

  The ECU isn't a DEC product, it's a industry-standard thing that we
  purchase.  Getting the ECU to work on a serial line has been a high
  priority, and I believe that the next release of it will work on a
  serial line.  The ECU was written for Windows, and of course, on a
  Windows system you *must* have graphics, and thus... a local KB.
  And because of this, DEC2000 systems have all been pretty much been
  sold with graphics (the RAID configuration utility *also* was a
  reason for the need for a graphics head).

  The current ECU will actually mostly work on a serial line, if you
  ignore some of the line-drawing stuff.  You need to monkey with the
  terminal settings so that they generate 8-bit escape sequences
  (if I remember correctly) to get the arrow & function keys to work.

  The whole problem seems to have been one of crossover pains from
  traditional "server" systems with no graphics, to PC derived systems
  which always include graphics.

