	The DB9 on the Sable (2100) has the same pinout as any standard PC 
serial port. 

	Pin # 	Signal Name

	  1       RLSD (Received Line Signal Detector) aka Carrier Detect
          2       RxD  (Received Data)
          3       TxD  (Transmitted Data)
          4       DTR  (Data Terminal Ready)
          5       GND  (Signal Common)
          6       DSR  (Data Set Ready)
          7    RTS/RFS (Request to Send or Ready for Sending)
          8       CTS  (Clear to Send)
          9       RI   (Ring Indicator)

	A quick look through the BOM for the Sable I/O board didn't turn give
any info on the UART. I will have to dig deeper to find out what UART type is
used. I will post what I find.

