> I am looking for a LAT driver (preferably freeware or shareware) to run on a 
> MS-DOS PC on a Novell 3.12 network which will use Kermit to access a remote 
> VMS host across an existing WAN.
-----------
	There isn't any free/shareware LAT driver that I have heard of.
They are all commercial. DEC has theirs in Pathworks, Meridian Tech has
SuperLAT. MS-DOS Kermit 3.14 (in beta) supports both, prior versions
supported only Pathworks. Note that LAT isn't routable so your WAN
connection must bridge LAT and that's not a swift idea. You might consider
Kermit's internal TCP/IP Telnet to talk to VMS hosts which (typically)
also support TCP/IP. Alternatively, regular DECnet packets can be used
from CTERM in Pathworks.
	Joe D.


