   Stock drives for all were the RD-series.  The RD53 and RD54
   were the most common drives.

|>what kind of memory do they take, and in what configurations?

    The VAXstation 2000 supported up to 14 megabytes.  The base
    system had 4 MB, and room for one additional memory module.
    8 (MS400-CA) and 4 (MS400-BA) MB memory modules were available.

    The II-series processors supported up to 16 MB of memory, had
    room for two memory modules, and had 1 MB on the CPU board.
    1, 2, 4 and 8 MB MS630-xx modules were available.

    Go for the maximum memory configuration available.

