    Take a serious look at the MicroVAX or VAXstation 3100
    series, or a VAXstation 4000 VLC.  These are more recent,
    accept SCSI peripherals, and are considerably smaller and
    considerably faster than the II/2000 series.

|>if possible, i'd like
|>to combine memory and hard drives between whichever of them are
|>compatible to come up with one working system.  so, can i put MV II
|>memory in a VS II, etc.

    II series memory is interchangeable.  RD-series drives
    are interchangeable, but should be reformatted when
    moved between the II and the 2000 series, or between
    two IIs with different RQDX controller revisions.  (And
    the RQDX controller might need a jumper reset to support
