>Yes, I've seen the numbers :-)   What I *really* want to know is, how
would you
>describe in words the differences between these machines? eg, "The
3000/700 is
>a large server-type machine with excellent I/O capabilities, while the
200
>4/233
>is basically a super-PC with the latest Alpha chip inside." (I have no
