  The keyboards and mice on these systems are PS2 compatable.  You
  should be able to plug in any j-random PS2 keyboard and mouse.  The
  LK411 keyboard (which is electrically a PS2 compatable, but has a
  LK401 layout) is, as far as I know, only available from DEC.  Of
  course, if you have a problem with a non-DEC part, you may need to
  reproduce it with the DEC part... since KB's and mice can have a
  lot of quirks.


>- Can I use an OEM ATI MACH64 graphics card instead of the
three-times-
