  The server and driver are not yet shipping on OSF and VMS.  I can't
  provide the exact dates that they will be generally available for
  OSF and VMS, but I will say that it's in the works (in fact, I'm
  using a 2mb CX card on my system right now).

  So for right now, the ZLX-E1 is the option of choice.


  The ZLXp-E has *no* relationship to the Mach64.  The ZLX is
  manufactured by DEC.  Perhaps the main ASIC is being manufactured
  by the same foundry, I'm not sure.  The ZLX appears priced for the
  workstation market, and is 2-3 times faster in most things than
  most other cards (like > 2million 10-pixel vectors, etc), as well
  as having low-end 3D primitives (flat shaded lines, z-buffering,
  etc).  The server also has many, many man years of optimization.
  You will see a xmark difference of about 2:1 between the two cards.

  You will *like* the ZLX-E1.  It is a *very* nice option.

