> is basically a super-PC with the latest Alpha chip inside."

The AlphaStation 200/4 233 is a mid-range workstation. The DEC 3000-700 is
a higher-end workstation. The main difference is that you can get higher
performance graphics options to the 3000-700 (today). The AlphaStation 4/233
may run Windows NT, the DEC 3000-700 does not (since it uses the TURBO
channel). I think the I/O capabilities are more or less the same. The PCI
bus on the AlphaStation 400 may be slightly faster.
